1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,404
Last lesson you wrote Python. Today your code meets real data.

2
00:00:04,954 --> 00:00:05,454
Files.

3
00:00:05,454 --> 00:00:05,872
JSON.

4
00:00:05,872 --> 00:00:06,289
YAML.

5
00:00:06,289 --> 00:00:06,622
CSV.

6
00:00:06,622 --> 00:00:08,791
And environment variables.

7
00:00:08,791 --> 00:00:14,213
The five places where data and settings hide in every DevOps job.

8
00:00:14,763 --> 00:00:19,435
Every demo is typed live on Ubuntu twenty-four oh four, so you can follow along.

9
00:00:21,485 --> 00:00:26,178
Why these five? Because almost every tool you will meet keeps its settings in one of them.

10
00:00:26,728 --> 00:00:31,315
Ansible, Kubernetes, Docker Compose and GitHub Actions all use YAML.

11
00:00:31,865 --> 00:00:37,902
APIs speak JSON. Exports from spreadsheets and monitoring tools arrive as CSV.

12
00:00:38,452 --> 00:00:42,463
And secrets and switches reach your program as environment variables.

13
00:00:43,013 --> 00:00:47,237
Read them safely, convert the types, and your script works on any machine.

14
00:00:49,287 --> 00:00:56,199
First, plain files. Here is a small script called files dot P Y. Type: cat files dot P Y.

15
00:00:56,749 --> 00:00:57,683
Three blocks,

16
00:00:57,683 --> 00:00:58,761
each with open,

17
00:00:58,761 --> 00:00:59,624
a file name,

18
00:00:59,624 --> 00:01:00,414
and a mode.

19
00:01:00,414 --> 00:01:01,061
W writes,

20
00:01:01,061 --> 00:01:02,642
and replaces the file.

21
00:01:02,642 --> 00:01:04,151
A appends to the end.

22
00:01:04,151 --> 00:01:05,085
With no mode,

23
00:01:05,085 --> 00:01:06,307
the file is read.

24
00:01:06,307 --> 00:01:09,110
The with block closes the file for you,

25
00:01:09,110 --> 00:01:10,834
even if something fails.

26
00:01:10,834 --> 00:01:11,337
Run it.

27
00:01:11,337 --> 00:01:12,703
Type: python three,

28
00:01:12,703 --> 00:01:13,709
files dot P Y.

29
00:01:14,259 --> 00:01:15,817
Both lines came back,

30
00:01:15,817 --> 00:01:17,228
read from the file.

31
00:01:17,228 --> 00:01:19,305
Now look at the file itself.

32
00:01:19,305 --> 00:01:21,235
Type: cat notes dot T X T.

33
00:01:21,785 --> 00:01:23,127
The same two lines.

34
00:01:23,127 --> 00:01:25,174
Use with open for every file,

35
00:01:25,174 --> 00:01:27,081
so files always get closed.

36
00:01:27,081 --> 00:01:29,764
And remember: W erases what was there,

37
00:01:29,764 --> 00:01:31,812
so choose the mode carefully.

38
00:01:33,862 --> 00:01:40,305
Next, JSON, the language of API s. Here is a small file. Type: cat servers dot jay son.

39
00:01:40,855 --> 00:01:42,367
Braces make an object,

40
00:01:42,367 --> 00:01:44,566
and square brackets make a list.

41
00:01:44,566 --> 00:01:47,796
They are exactly Python dictionaries and lists.

42
00:01:47,796 --> 00:01:48,689
Start Python.

43
00:01:48,689 --> 00:01:49,995
Type: python three,

44
00:01:49,995 --> 00:01:50,476
dash Q.

45
00:01:51,326 --> 00:01:54,889
Import the jay son module. Type: import jay son.

46
00:01:55,439 --> 00:01:57,433
Load the file into Python.

47
00:01:57,433 --> 00:01:58,047
Type: d,

48
00:01:58,047 --> 00:01:58,584
equals,

49
00:01:58,584 --> 00:01:59,889
jay son dot load,

50
00:01:59,889 --> 00:02:00,272
open,

51
00:02:00,272 --> 00:02:01,807
servers dot jay son,

52
00:02:01,807 --> 00:02:03,801
then two closing brackets.

53
00:02:04,351 --> 00:02:05,387
Nothing printed,

54
00:02:05,387 --> 00:02:07,005
but d now holds the data.

55
00:02:07,005 --> 00:02:07,458
Dig in.

56
00:02:07,458 --> 00:02:07,976
Type: d,

57
00:02:07,976 --> 00:02:08,947
square bracket,

58
00:02:08,947 --> 00:02:10,242
quote servers quote,

59
00:02:10,242 --> 00:02:11,601
close square bracket,

60
00:02:11,601 --> 00:02:12,572
square bracket,

61
00:02:12,572 --> 00:02:12,831
one,

62
00:02:12,831 --> 00:02:14,190
close square bracket,

63
00:02:14,190 --> 00:02:15,161
square bracket,

64
00:02:15,161 --> 00:02:16,261
quote name quote,

65
00:02:16,261 --> 00:02:17,621
close square bracket.

66
00:02:18,171 --> 00:02:18,731
Web two.

67
00:02:18,731 --> 00:02:19,152
A key,

68
00:02:19,152 --> 00:02:19,923
a position,

69
00:02:19,923 --> 00:02:21,115
then another key.

70
00:02:21,115 --> 00:02:22,587
Now go the other way,

71
00:02:22,587 --> 00:02:23,989
from Python to text.

72
00:02:23,989 --> 00:02:25,671
Type: jay son dot dumps,

73
00:02:25,671 --> 00:02:26,021
open,

74
00:02:26,021 --> 00:02:26,162
d,

75
00:02:26,162 --> 00:02:27,213
square bracket,

76
00:02:27,213 --> 00:02:28,615
quote servers quote,

77
00:02:28,615 --> 00:02:29,666
square bracket,

78
00:02:29,666 --> 00:02:30,017
zero,

79
00:02:30,017 --> 00:02:31,489
close square bracket,

80
00:02:31,489 --> 00:02:31,909
close.

81
00:02:32,459 --> 00:02:37,622
Text, ready to send to an API. Leave Python. Type: exit, open, close.

82
00:02:38,172 --> 00:02:38,740
JSON in,

83
00:02:38,740 --> 00:02:40,374
dictionaries and lists.

84
00:02:40,374 --> 00:02:42,293
Dictionaries and lists out.

85
00:02:42,293 --> 00:02:43,642
Use load for files,

86
00:02:43,642 --> 00:02:45,703
and loads with an S for text.

87
00:02:47,753 --> 00:02:48,123
Next,

88
00:02:48,123 --> 00:02:48,493
YAML,

89
00:02:48,493 --> 00:02:50,121
the format of Ansible,

90
00:02:50,121 --> 00:02:52,341
Kubernetes and Docker Compose.

91
00:02:52,341 --> 00:02:53,968
Here is a config file.

92
00:02:53,968 --> 00:02:55,966
Type: cat config dot yamel.

93
00:02:56,516 --> 00:02:58,262
No braces and no quotes.

94
00:02:58,262 --> 00:03:00,372
Indentation is the structure,

95
00:03:00,372 --> 00:03:01,609
just like Python,

96
00:03:01,609 --> 00:03:03,791
and a dash starts a list item.

97
00:03:03,791 --> 00:03:04,737
Start Python.

98
00:03:04,737 --> 00:03:06,119
Type: python three,

99
00:03:06,119 --> 00:03:06,628
dash Q.

100
00:03:07,478 --> 00:03:08,936
YAML is not built in.

101
00:03:08,936 --> 00:03:11,089
It needs the pie yamel package,

102
00:03:11,089 --> 00:03:15,879
installed with pip install pie yamel inside your virtual environment.

103
00:03:15,879 --> 00:03:17,893
It is already installed here.

104
00:03:17,893 --> 00:03:19,212
Type: import yamel.

105
00:03:19,762 --> 00:03:20,877
Load the file.

106
00:03:20,877 --> 00:03:22,549
Always use safe load.

107
00:03:22,549 --> 00:03:23,345
Type: cfg,

108
00:03:23,345 --> 00:03:23,903
equals,

109
00:03:23,903 --> 00:03:26,371
yamel dot safe underscore load,

110
00:03:26,371 --> 00:03:26,769
open,

111
00:03:26,769 --> 00:03:28,123
config dot yamel,

112
00:03:28,123 --> 00:03:30,194
then two closing brackets.

113
00:03:30,744 --> 00:03:36,866
Now ask for the limit. Type: cfg, square bracket, quote limit quote, close square bracket.

114
00:03:37,416 --> 00:03:37,927
Eighty,

115
00:03:37,927 --> 00:03:39,676
and it is a real number,

116
00:03:39,676 --> 00:03:40,332
not text.

117
00:03:40,332 --> 00:03:41,863
YAML keeps the types.

118
00:03:41,863 --> 00:03:42,884
Now the hosts.

119
00:03:42,884 --> 00:03:43,613
Type: cfg,

120
00:03:43,613 --> 00:03:44,707
square bracket,

121
00:03:44,707 --> 00:03:46,019
quote hosts quote,

122
00:03:46,019 --> 00:03:47,550
close square bracket.

123
00:03:48,100 --> 00:03:52,110
A Python list. Leave Python. Type: exit, open, close.

124
00:03:52,660 --> 00:03:54,866
Safe load builds only plain data.

125
00:03:54,866 --> 00:03:58,877
The plain load function can run code from an untrusted file,

126
00:03:58,877 --> 00:03:59,679
so avoid it.

127
00:04:01,729 --> 00:04:07,702
Now CSV, the format of spreadsheets and exports. Type: cat servers dot C S V.

128
00:04:08,252 --> 00:04:13,756
A header row, then one row per server. Start Python. Type: python three, dash Q.

129
00:04:14,306 --> 00:04:18,018
Import the C S V module. Type: import C S V.

130
00:04:18,568 --> 00:04:20,835
Read the rows as dictionaries,

131
00:04:20,835 --> 00:04:21,818
one per line.

132
00:04:21,818 --> 00:04:22,649
Type: rows,

133
00:04:22,649 --> 00:04:23,178
equals,

134
00:04:23,178 --> 00:04:23,556
list,

135
00:04:23,556 --> 00:04:24,538
open bracket,

136
00:04:24,538 --> 00:04:26,201
C S V dot Dict Reader,

137
00:04:26,201 --> 00:04:27,183
open bracket,

138
00:04:27,183 --> 00:04:27,561
open,

139
00:04:27,561 --> 00:04:28,544
open bracket,

140
00:04:28,544 --> 00:04:29,904
servers dot C S V,

141
00:04:29,904 --> 00:04:31,944
and three closing brackets.

142
00:04:32,494 --> 00:04:36,782
Nothing printed. How many rows? Type: len, open, rows, close.

143
00:04:37,332 --> 00:04:38,231
Four servers.

144
00:04:38,231 --> 00:04:39,822
Look at the second one.

145
00:04:39,822 --> 00:04:40,582
Type: rows,

146
00:04:40,582 --> 00:04:41,620
square bracket,

147
00:04:41,620 --> 00:04:41,896
one,

148
00:04:41,896 --> 00:04:43,348
close square bracket.

149
00:04:43,898 --> 00:04:44,947
Spot the trap.

150
00:04:44,947 --> 00:04:46,669
The C P U is in quotes.

151
00:04:46,669 --> 00:04:48,766
C S V always gives you text.

152
00:04:48,766 --> 00:04:49,590
Convert it.

153
00:04:49,590 --> 00:04:50,338
Type: int,

154
00:04:50,338 --> 00:04:50,713
open,

155
00:04:50,713 --> 00:04:51,087
rows,

156
00:04:51,087 --> 00:04:52,210
square bracket,

157
00:04:52,210 --> 00:04:52,510
one,

158
00:04:52,510 --> 00:04:54,083
close square bracket,

159
00:04:54,083 --> 00:04:55,206
square bracket,

160
00:04:55,206 --> 00:04:56,554
quote C P U quote,

161
00:04:56,554 --> 00:04:58,126
close square bracket,

162
00:04:58,126 --> 00:04:58,576
close.

163
00:04:59,126 --> 00:05:03,712
Ninety-one, a real number. Leave Python. Type: exit, open, close.

164
00:05:04,262 --> 00:05:06,290
Rule: CSV always gives text.

165
00:05:06,290 --> 00:05:06,869
As text,

166
00:05:06,869 --> 00:05:09,114
nine is bigger than ninety-one,

167
00:05:09,114 --> 00:05:11,793
so always convert before you compare.

168
00:05:13,843 --> 00:05:14,401
Finally,

169
00:05:14,401 --> 00:05:15,935
environment variables.

170
00:05:15,935 --> 00:05:19,562
This is how secrets and switches reach your program,

171
00:05:19,562 --> 00:05:21,446
without living in the code.

172
00:05:21,446 --> 00:05:22,910
Set one in the shell.

173
00:05:22,910 --> 00:05:25,491
Type: export L I M I T equals eighty.

174
00:05:26,041 --> 00:05:30,073
Set, silently. Start Python. Type: python three, dash Q.

175
00:05:30,623 --> 00:05:33,951
Import the O S module. Type: import O S.

176
00:05:34,501 --> 00:05:40,090
Read the variable. Type: O S dot getenv, open, quote L I M I T quote, close.

177
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:41,181
Eighty,

178
00:05:41,181 --> 00:05:42,261
but in quotes.

179
00:05:42,261 --> 00:05:45,194
Environment variables are always text.

180
00:05:45,194 --> 00:05:46,275
Add a default,

181
00:05:46,275 --> 00:05:47,201
and convert.

182
00:05:47,201 --> 00:05:47,973
Type: int,

183
00:05:47,973 --> 00:05:48,359
open,

184
00:05:48,359 --> 00:05:49,516
O S dot getenv,

185
00:05:49,516 --> 00:05:49,902
open,

186
00:05:49,902 --> 00:05:51,600
quote L I M I T quote,

187
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:52,063
comma,

188
00:05:52,063 --> 00:05:53,453
quote fifty quote,

189
00:05:53,453 --> 00:05:53,916
close,

190
00:05:53,916 --> 00:05:54,379
close.

191
00:05:54,929 --> 00:05:55,448
Eighty.

192
00:05:55,448 --> 00:05:57,597
If the variable were missing,

193
00:05:57,597 --> 00:05:59,524
the default would be used.

194
00:05:59,524 --> 00:06:01,821
Try a variable that is missing.

195
00:06:01,821 --> 00:06:03,377
Type: O S dot getenv,

196
00:06:03,377 --> 00:06:03,748
open,

197
00:06:03,748 --> 00:06:05,526
quote R E G I O N quote,

198
00:06:05,526 --> 00:06:05,971
comma,

199
00:06:05,971 --> 00:06:08,564
quote E U dash west dash one quote,

200
00:06:08,564 --> 00:06:09,009
close.

201
00:06:09,559 --> 00:06:10,425
The default,

202
00:06:10,425 --> 00:06:12,372
so the program still works.

203
00:06:12,372 --> 00:06:13,598
But for a secret,

204
00:06:13,598 --> 00:06:15,330
you want a loud failure.

205
00:06:15,330 --> 00:06:16,917
Type: O S dot environ,

206
00:06:16,917 --> 00:06:17,999
square bracket,

207
00:06:17,999 --> 00:06:19,586
quote T O K E N quote,

208
00:06:19,586 --> 00:06:21,100
close square bracket.

209
00:06:21,650 --> 00:06:22,407
A key error.

210
00:06:22,407 --> 00:06:24,990
A missing secret should stop the program,

211
00:06:24,990 --> 00:06:25,936
not be guessed.

212
00:06:25,936 --> 00:06:29,465
And never type a real secret into a script or a command,

213
00:06:29,465 --> 00:06:31,229
and never commit one to git.

214
